Description: automatic NVIDIA GPU undervolting, overclocking and per-game tuning
 PenguinBurner tunes NVIDIA GPUs on Linux automatically. One Auto-UV scan
 sweeps the card under a managed headless Q2RTX benchmark plus a CUDA load,
 verifies stability and FPS per watt at single voltage/frequency bin precision,
 and saves three profiles: Efficiency, Balanced and Performance (undervolt plus
 overclock). On a verified RTX 5080 the Balanced tier held roughly the stock
 loaded clock at 272 W instead of 341 W.
 .
 Features:
  * Adaptive undervolting that switches between the saved tiers while you
    play to hold your frame-rate target, and eases off on frame caps and
    idle desktops.
  * A Game Library that brings Steam, Lutris and Heroic games into one list,
    each with its own GPU profile, adaptive FPS target and overlay setting,
    applied at launch and restored on exit.
  * An in-game Vulkan overlay showing base FPS, frame-generation FPS, PC
    latency, clocks, power, temperatures and the active tier.
  * Manual V/F and fan curve editors, an automatic silent fan curve, MSI
    Afterburner profile import and LACT config export.
  * A Qt desktop UI and a CLI, both driving one root systemd service
    (penguin-burnerd, a compiled Rust daemon) installed once with a single
    admin prompt.
 .
 Pre-optimized Auto-UV targets are included for RTX 30, 40 and 50 series cards.
 GPU tuning can crash the driver or freeze the system; use it at your own risk.
